Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 11:46:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix(client): render surface replacements no Definition
 claims
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An unclaimed surface replacement rendered as nothing in the chat view.
The message Definition matches append-origin events plus compaction's own
checkpoint, identified by hardcoded plugin name, and the sole fallback
matched append origin only, so a user/message replacement from any other
producer was claimed by no Definition and caught by no fallback.

Extend that one fallback instead of adding a second: the registry admits
exactly one and throws on a duplicate, and the assembler consults it only
when no ordinary Definition claimed the target. UnknownSurfaceNode gains
an optional replaced list of shadowed seqs, read from sourceEventSeqs,
and the renderer reports the shadowed history rather than presenting the
replacement as an ordinary message — a landed replacement must not erase
a transcript the reader already saw.

Append-origin fallback stays unreachable through an assembled window
because all three SurfaceEventType members have owning Definitions, so
that arm is asserted at the Definition level.
